  keeps:
    word: keeps
    frequency_rank: 5
    definition: Holds onto, maintains, or continues something, from a promise to a possession; also the stronghold
      at the heart of a castle, or the provisions needed to support someone. Chiefly in the phrase for keeps, meaning
      permanently.
    pos_primary: verb
    pos: verb; noun
    origin: feed
  says:
    word: say
    frequency_rank: 6
    definition: To speak words aloud; to state or assert; of a text, sign, or instrument, to convey information.
      As a noun, the right or chance to influence a decision; as an adverb, approximately or for example.
    pos_primary: verb
    pos: verb; noun; adverb; interjection
    origin: feed
  lack:
    word: lack
    frequency_rank: 5
    definition: An absence or shortage of something needed or wanted; as a verb, to be without something or to have
      too little of it.
    pos_primary: noun
    pos: noun; verb
    origin: feed
  enables:
    word: enable
    frequency_rank: 4
    definition: To give someone the ability, means, or authority to do something, or to make some action possible.
    pos_primary: verb
    pos: verb
    origin: feed
  holds:
    word: hold
    frequency_rank: 5
    definition: To grasp, contain, or keep possession of something, from a hand holding a cup to a shelf holding
      books. As a noun it can be a grip, a place where animals or prisoners are kept, or a ship's cargo space below
      deck.
    pos_primary: verb
    pos: verb; noun
    origin: feed
  feeds:
    word: feed
    frequency_rank: 5
    definition: To give food to someone or an animal, or to eat; as a noun, food given to non-human animals, or
      any material supplied continuously into a system.
    pos_primary: verb
    pos: verb; noun
    origin: feed
  follows:
    word: follow
    frequency_rank: 5
    definition: To go or come after a person or thing; to pursue; to happen or come next in sequence; to obey or
      act in accordance with; to understand the sense of, as in following an argument.
    pos_primary: verb
    pos: verb; noun
    origin: feed
  harms:
    word: harm
    frequency_rank: 4
    definition: Injury or damage, physical or emotional, and as a verb, the act of causing it.
    pos_primary: noun
    pos: noun; verb
    origin: feed
  assumed:
    word: assumed
    frequency_rank: 4
    definition: Adopted, especially a name or identity, in order to deceive or conceal; also, more broadly, supposed
      to be true without being checked.
    pos_primary: verb
    pos: verb; adjective
    origin: feed
  unclear:
    word: unclear
    frequency_rank: 4
    definition: Not clearly stated, understood, or seen; open to more than one reading. Instructions can be unclear
      on paper just as a foggy road is unclear to the eye.
    pos_primary: adjective
    pos: adjective
    origin: feed
